{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>יזיד</b> Two times in the Masorah; the other: אך הנביא אשר יזיד לדבר דבר בשמי — meaning: if the prophet presumptuously speaks a word I did not command him, he is like one who kills his fellow, like the prophet at Bethel who caused the prophet who came with the word of HaShem to turn back and lied to him, and caused him to be killed." "<b>על רעהו</b> Five times in the Masorah: (a) here; (b) כאשר יקום איש על רעהו; (c) ושעיר על רעהו יקרא in Isaiah — כי מפלת אדום כה תאמרו איש על רעהו; (d) as in Jeremiah, on the matter of false prophets — גבר מחליק על רעהו — meaning: one who flatters his fellow with smooth lips and prophesies false prophecy to him, flattering him with words, is as though he destroys him; and this is ושעיר על רעהו יקרא, as if he killed him; and this is ורצחו נפש." "<b>בערמה</b> Two times in the Masorah: here, and the other: ויעשו גם המה בערמה, in the Gibeonites. This one who presumptuously schemed to kill בערמה and distanced himself from the congregation of Israel — therefore מעם מזבחי תקחנו למות. But the Gibeonites, who acted בערמה and drew near to the congregation of Israel, merited to be woodcutters and water-drawers for the altar. This one distanced himself from the altar; those drew near to the altar. Thus says our master the Rosh, of blessed memory."], :book :exodus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {1 "The Ba'al HaTurim lists five occurrences but enumerates only four distinct citations; the fifth is not explicitly separated in the text."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:13:56.783397244Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}